From 2e6a42260d5fd616e814e2176a29a82458a163e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pengdonglin <pengdonglin@xiaomi.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:41:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] fix(session): preserve whitespace in captured executable
 and library paths

Parse only the fixed /proc/maps header with scanf and keep its complete
pathname remainder when recording, annotating and reading session maps.
Bound protection fields and allow space for a PATH_MAX pathname plus its
mapping header and optional build-id suffix.

Recognize a bounded hexadecimal build-id trailer only at the end of the
saved pathname. Emit an explicit empty trailer for ELF objects without a
build ID so a legitimate filename ending in build-id:deadbeef is not
mistaken for metadata. Preserve tabs and trailing spaces in filenames.

Add native map-reader coverage for ordinary/whitespace library names,
legacy mappings without a trailer, explicit empty IDs, long paths and a
final line without a newline. Real FuncGraph recording regressions also
exercise Unicode filenames, offline export after moving the executable
or shared library, typed arguments, return values and source positions.
